      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083460/assets/22a909d34b63517bf5ccf90560a8070d20e1aa91a6c9eaf8f4e5326208b9d751.png)\n\n \n\nThe shell above is obtained by rotating the curve $y=2{x}^{2}$ for $x\\in [0,1]$ by $2\\pi $ radians about the $x$-axis, as shown above. For each point $(x,y,z)$ on the shell, the charge density (electric charge per unit surface area) of the shell is given by the function \n\n$$\nd(x,y,z)=\\frac{x({y}^{2}+{z}^{2})}{\\sqrt{16{x}^{2}+1}}.\n$$",
